We have a small race here, since we execute the reroute asynchronously after updating the desired nodes, it's possible to break the invariants in:
```
    private void reroute(RoutingAllocation allocation) {
        assert hasDeadNodes(allocation) == false : "dead nodes should be explicitly cleaned up. See disassociateDeadNodes";
        assert AutoExpandReplicas.getAutoExpandReplicaChanges(allocation.metadata(), () -> allocation).isEmpty()
            : "auto-expand replicas out of sync with number of nodes in the cluster";
```
i.e: if we execute a reroute after updating the desired nodes, the test fail.

I haven't checked if we have the same issues just after adding a new node, but I think it might be possible?

